  "narrative": "Wellington R.1037 was on a training sortie from RAF Chipping Warden, Northamptonshire, operated by 12 Operational Training Unit, which prepared aircrew for frontline bomber service. On 20 October 1941, the aircraft came down near the station itself. Those aboard included crew members Brumby, Newton, Jenner, Brathwaite, and Crompton, among others. Two of the crew were killed; three survived. The cause of the crash is not recorded in the available sources.",
